# .env.example — every credential the runtime leaves this machine with.
#
# Copy it and fill in what you have:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#     python3 scripts/rehearse.py --env-file .env --require-all
#
# A filled-in `.env` is gitignored (see .gitignore) and this repository is
# public, so the file must never be committed. `--env-file` is explicit: the
# rehearsal never discovers a credential file on its own, so a stray `.env`
# cannot change what a report says about the environment it was given.
#
# An ALREADY-SET environment variable wins over a line here, which makes one run
# overridable without editing the file:
#
#     GEMINI_API_KEY=other python3 scripts/rehearse.py --env-file .env
#
# Rules: `KEY=VALUE` only — no `export`, no interpolation, no multi-line values.
# A malformed line is refused by name and line number rather than skipped, so a
# typo cannot read as a `missing` row. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# A `missing` row in the rehearsal is not a defect: it means this checkout is not
# configured for that surface. `invalid` is a credential that is set and
# REJECTED, and that is the one state a release must not proceed past. Which
# surface each variable unlocks is in SETUP.md → Production credentials.
#
# ── The model ladder (rungs are tried in this order) ─────────────────────────
# rung 1 — Google AI Studio, free tier: https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
# Either name works; GEMINI_API_KEY is the one the workflows pass.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# rung 2 — the `opencode` CLI's own providers. The CLI must also be installed
# (`npm install -g opencode-ai`); a key alone does not make this rung work.
OPENCODE_ZEN_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# rung 3 — OpenRouter: https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# ── Phase 0 search backends (order: exa-mcp, then tinyfish) ──────────────────
# https://dashboard.exa.ai  |  https://www.tinyfish.ai
EXA_API_KEY=
TINYFISH_API_KEY=

# ── Render ladder, rung 1 (the hosted escape hatch for SPAs like magenta.tv) ─
# https://www.firecrawl.dev
FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=

# ── Optional: the YouTube Data API path. The HTML live filter needs no key. ──
# https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/youtube.googleapis.com
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

# ── The Google Calendar the runtime drives, via Composio ─────────────────────
# API key: https://app.composio.dev
COMPOSIO_API_KEY=
# Set EXACTLY ONE of these two: the Composio user handle (survives a reconnect)
# or a pinned connected-account id. Setting both is an ambiguity the rehearsal
# reports as `invalid` rather than guessing whose calendar to read.
COMPOSIO_USER_ID=
COMPOSIO_CONNECTED_ACCOUNT_ID=
# The calendar address itself. In the workflows this is a repository VARIABLE
# (`BASKETBALL_CALENDAR_ID`), not a secret; here it is just a value.
BASKETBALL_CALENDAR_ID=

# ── Filing issues (the self-improvement and corpus-flip loops) ───────────────
# A classic token with `repo` scope, or a fine-grained one with Issues: write:
# https://github.com/settings/tokens
GITHUB_TOKEN=
# `gh`'s own variable name; either one is read.
GH_TOKEN=
